## DotnetDevelopmentComponent

**Selector:** `app-dotnet-development`  
**Location:** `src/app/features/docs/components/dotnet-development/`  
**Feature:** `docs`

A standalone documentation page component for the `.NET Development` guide. Displays structured content covering how to use Cyréna's `cyrena.dotnet` extension for .NET development.

### Component State

All data is stored as `readonly` class properties (no signals needed — static reference content):

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `extensionId` | `string` | `'cyrena.dotnet'` — the extension identifier |
| `prerequisites` | `string[]` | 3 prerequisite items: .NET SDK, IDE, extension installed |
| `projectTypes` | `ProjectType[]` | 6 supported C# project templates |
| `baseFolders` | `FolderEntry[]` | 8 base folder/file entries with read-only status |
| `blazorFolders` | `BlazorFolder[]` | 7 Blazor-specific folder entries |
| `mvcFolders` | `MvcFolder[]` | 5 MVC-specific folder entries |
| `steps` | `Step[]` | 6-step workflow guide |

### Interfaces

```typescript
interface ProjectType {
  name: string;
  description: string;
}

interface FolderEntry {
  name: string;
  purpose: string;
  readOnly: boolean;
}

interface BlazorFolder {
  name: string;
  content: string;
  readOnly: boolean;
}

interface MvcFolder {
  name: string;
  content: string;
  readOnly: boolean;
}

interface Step {
  number: number;
  title: string;
  description: string;
}
```

### Page Sections (Template)

1. **Prerequisites** — bullet list of 3 requirements
2. **Supported Project Types** — table of 6 project types with descriptions
3. **Opinionated Structure Note** — info alert about keeping default folder layout
4. **Default Folder Structure** — table with Folder/File, Purpose, Read-Only columns
5. **Blazor Additional Folders** — table of Blazor-specific folders
6. **MVC Additional Folders** — table of MVC-specific folders
7. **Recommended Workflow** — intro paragraph + 6 numbered steps
8. **Permissions Note** — callout box summarizing read-only vs writable rules

### Styling

Uses component-scoped CSS with dark-themed Bootstrap tables:
- `.table-dark` — semi-transparent dark background, light borders
- `.alert-info` — cyan-tinted info box
- `.permissions-note` — green-tinted callout
- `.step-number` — 40px circular numbered badges
- Read-only badges: `bg-danger` (red), Writable badges: `bg-success` (green)

### Route

Registered at `/docs/dotnet` under the `DocLayoutComponent`.

### Sidebar Entry

```typescript
{
  id: 'dotnet',
  title: '.NET Development',
  description: 'Build .NET projects with Cyrena',
  route: '/docs/dotnet',
  icon: 'bi-filetype-cs'
}
```

### Key Content Rules

- Project/solution files (`.csproj`, `.sln`, `.slnx`) are **read-only** — AI cannot edit them
- `wwwroot/css` and `wwwroot/js` are **fully readable and writable**
- `.json` config files are **read-only** in Blazor and MVC projects
- Root-level `.cs` files are editable but AI cannot create new ones there
- Folder layout is opinionated; deviating requires a custom extension
